{"sourceSha256": "18a25ce95fb126cbbfe02ae15a29e9d54af000ab68036cfb62a70832aed514ba", "text": "Benchmark\n\netcotion Soh tors Ticket Id:\n08/07/2018\n\nCommunity Nurse\nCommunity Health Centre\nWoodville\n\nDear Sir/Madam,\n\nRe: Ms. Monica Osborn, 69-years-old\n\n1 am writing to request for the continuity of care for Ms. Osburn, a long term patient of ours since 2003,\nwho was diagnosed with hypertension and depression, She will be re-locating to Woodville per daughter's\n\nrequest and will need regular monitoring to facilitate her continued care.\n\nMs. Osburn has had hypertension for ten years and has been diagnosed with depression in 2008. She has\n\nbeen taking anti-hypertensive and anti-depressant medications but experiences periodic problems in the\nadministration of her own medicines. Moreover, the patient has had a long history of alcoholism that\nbecomes more excessive with anxiety.\n\nSocially, Ms. Osburn is divorced, lives alone and depends solely on her pension for income. Such\ncircumstance has led her only married daughter to request Ms. Osburn to move to Woodville for her to be\ncloser with the said patient.\n\nit would be greatly appreciated if you could regularly monitor Ms. Osburn once she settles in Woodville.\nThis is to ensure her compliance with her medication regimen and to also keep a close watch on her\nalcohol intake and diet. Please encourage the patient to be in family and social activities such as the Elderly\nCitizens’ Club. Furthermore, could you please contact her attending physician upon her arrival?\n\nThank you for taking over in the management of Ms. Osburn,\nShould you have any more queries, do not hesitate to ask.\nYours faithfully,\n\nClaudel Marie Sayson\nNurse\nNewport Community Health Centre\n\nReport\n\nThis is a good letter with appropriate selection of\ncase notes and logical paragraphing. There is good\n\ncoherence throughout. Mistakes pertaining to\ngrammar are visible. However, these do not reduce\ncommunication.\n\nEstimated Grade B+\n\nAdvice 1. Revise grammar.\n2. Keep up the good work!\n\n256 Henley Beach Ad, Underdale, $032\nhitow!/wrenw benchmark edu.com.au/oet writing-corection\nwow benchmar ied com gu /pteoetielts\n\nComment (bachirict J: 69 yeors old\n\nComment (bnchmrk2}: vee", "pages": [{"number": 1, "text": "Benchmark\n\netcotion Soh tors Ticket Id:\n08/07/2018\n\nCommunity Nurse\nCommunity Health Centre\nWoodville\n\nDear Sir/Madam,\n\nRe: Ms. Monica Osborn, 69-years-old\n\n1 am writing to request for the continuity of care for Ms. Osburn, a long term patient of ours since 2003,\nwho was diagnosed with hypertension and depression, She will be re-locating to Woodville per daughter's\n\nrequest and will need regular monitoring to facilitate her continued care.\n\nMs. Osburn has had hypertension for ten years and has been diagnosed with depression in 2008. She has\n\nbeen taking anti-hypertensive and anti-depressant medications but experiences periodic problems in the\nadministration of her own medicines. Moreover, the patient has had a long history of alcoholism that\nbecomes more excessive with anxiety.\n\nSocially, Ms. Osburn is divorced, lives alone and depends solely on her pension for income. Such\ncircumstance has led her only married daughter to request Ms. Osburn to move to Woodville for her to be\ncloser with the said patient.\n\nit would be greatly appreciated if you could regularly monitor Ms. Osburn once she settles in Woodville.\nThis is to ensure her compliance with her medication regimen and to also keep a close watch on her\nalcohol intake and diet. Please encourage the patient to be in family and social activities such as the Elderly\nCitizens’ Club. Furthermore, could you please contact her attending physician upon her arrival?\n\nThank you for taking over in the management of Ms. Osburn,\nShould you have any more queries, do not hesitate to ask.\nYours faithfully,\n\nClaudel Marie Sayson\nNurse\nNewport Community Health Centre\n\nReport\n\nThis is a 